The Euler–Lagrange equation gives $\frac{d}{dt}\frac{\partial L}{\partial\dot x}
  =
  \frac{\partial L}{\partial x},$ or $\boxed{\ddot x=-\omega^2x.}$ Its general real solution is $x(t)=A\cos\omega t+B\sin\omega t.$ Twice differentiating either sinusoid returns the function multiplied by $-\omega^2$, so the frequency in the potential is exactly the frequency of the motion.

