p.src:
The asymptotic form suggests a Gaussian: $\psi_0(x)=C\exp\left(-\frac{\omega x^2}{2\hbar}\right),$ where $\omega>0$ denotes the positive oscillator frequency. Its first two derivatives are $\begin{aligned}
  \psi_0'
  &=-\frac{\omega x}{\hbar}\psi_0,\\
  \psi_0''
  &=
  \left(
    \frac{\omega^2x^2}{\hbar^2}
    -\frac{\omega}{\hbar}
  \right)\psi_0.
  \end{aligned}$

