p.src:
Applying the Hamiltonian, $\begin{aligned}
  \hat H\psi_0
  &=
  -\frac{\hbar^2}{2}
  \left(
    \frac{\omega^2x^2}{\hbar^2}
    -\frac{\omega}{\hbar}
  \right)\psi_0
  +
  \frac12\omega^2x^2\psi_0\\
  &=
  \frac12\hbar\omega\,\psi_0.
  \end{aligned}$ The two terms proportional to $x^2$ cancel, leaving $\boxed{E_0=\frac12\hbar\omega.}$

